- **Merged identity.** I merged three addresses into one person, Graham Campbell. This is a guess from names and addresses, and nothing was written to `.mailmap`. Unmerged, the rows are:
  - `<email redacted>`: 403 lines (34.0%)
  - `<email redacted>`: 377 lines (31.8%)
  - `<email redacted>`: 2 lines (0.2%)
- **`root` and `Your Name`.** These look like default git identities. From `git log`, `root` made the commit "fix" (7007c6e) and `Your Name` made "compat shims" (b39e8d9). They are probably the same person who made the Aiko-era changes, but I can't tell who that is from the history.
- **Bus factor.** The bus factor is 1 for the whole of `src/Parser`: Graham alone holds 65.9% of the surviving lines. It takes 2 authors to reach 80%. The bus factor here is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50%.

## What the numbers leave out
- **Dropped file.** `src/Parser/Unicode/CharTable.php` (431 lines) is generated, so I left it out of every number. If you audit that file, its generator and inputs matter more than its author.
- **Reformat and rewrite commits.** I checked for mechanical rewrites across 48 commits and set none aside. There was no reformat commit to ignore.
- **Copy detection.** The figures use `-w -M -C`. Copy detection moved 80 lines to other authors. Without it, Graham's merged share is 66.7% (792 lines) instead of 65.9% (782). Vance Lucas's 10 lines exist only because of copy detection, so those lines were copied in from elsewhere.

## `Lexer.php`
It has 58 lines, and all of them are Graham Campbell's, counting the same three addresses as one person:
- `<email redacted>`: 52 lines (89.7%), last commit 2020-06-07, inactive.
- `<email redacted>`: 6 lines (10.3%), last commit 2026-08-24, active.
- `<email redacted>`: 0 lines.

Graham made the first commit on 2020-06-07. About 20 of the 58 lines (34.5%) were written elsewhere and moved here, mostly from `src/Loader/Lines.php`, `src/Value.php` and `src/Loader/Value.php`. Graham wrote those too, but you may want to read those source files for context.

## Escape handling
`src/Parser/Escape.php` is 206 lines, all by Aiko Tanaka (100%), in 2 commits ("Add escape sequence handling" and "Escape: more sequences", both 2026-08-26). Aiko is active, but Aiko has only one day of history in this repo. `EntryParser.php` also references escapes, and Graham holds most of that file.

For an audit, the escape code is also the newest code and has a single author. It is the part that most needs independent review.

These counts show whose code survives. They say nothing about quality or about who understands the code best.
